# The manual checklist drives `docs/manual-acceptance.sk`, and this is the one thing about it that a
# player would otherwise have to notice by hand: whether the `/acc <x>` dispatcher reads its argument.
#
# Skript command arguments are `arg-1`, `arg-2`, … (`arg-<type>` for a typed one) -- not `{_name}`
# variables. Reading the wrong thing fails silently in the worst way: every command falls through to the
# help text and no menu ever opens, which is exactly what a first version of that script did.
#
# `argcheck` is a branch of the dispatcher that only writes a log line, so running it needs no player and
# opens no window. The console runs the command here and the verifier requires the line it logs.
on load:
    execute console command "/acc argcheck"
